<title>ISRAEL: Russia seeks to supply Israel with gas, oil.</title>
<headline>Russia seeks to supply Israel with gas, oil.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian Prime Minister Viktor Chernomyrdin telephoned Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Monday and said Russia wanted to sign deals to supply gas and oil to the Jewish state.</p>
<p>&quot;Mr. Chernomyrdin expressed Russia's desire...to further economic ties between the two countries, including deals on the provision of oil and gas from Russia to Israel,&quot; Netanyahu's spokesman Shai Bazak said in a statement.</p>
<p>Israel has been seeking to diversify its energy sources, particularly natural gas.</p>
<p>Netanyahu accepted an invitation from Chernomyrdin to visit Russia. The trip was slated for early 1997, the spokesman said.</p>
